  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-27 by an independent auditor who authored none of the change, after 9b7673180c and 5a65ff5ee7 (spec-add-path-limit-send-receive). RFC 7911 Section 2: \"A BGP speaker that re-advertises a route MUST generate its own Path Identifier to be associated with the re-advertised route.\" The moved producers are session_write.go writeUpdateBody (calls the extracted s.pathsLimit.filter and owes PATHS-LIMIT elections after commit) and session_ownership.go adjOutWrite.allow (a pathsLimitDemotion recovery item may withdraw a current owner's ADD-PATH key). Neither generates an identifier: a survivor the election re-announces goes through the ordinary staged forward rail, whose identifier still comes only from forward_path_id.go, forward_body.go and forward_provenance.go, all byte-identical, as are all 19 tagged units. The positives still assert the re-advertised identifier differs from the received one and is stable per destination; the negatives still fail on a received-id passthrough, each with a verified revert or mutant record. Verdict unchanged: enforced. Earlier judgements are in this file's git history. The same closure added a doc-comment paragraph to session_ownership.go beginAdjOut stating that the table mutex stays held until release and MUST NOT be taken again inside that window; the function body is unchanged.",
